WHY GPL-2.0-OR-LATER, AND WHAT IS DERIVED

This project drives the ASUS ROG Claymore's lighting by speaking its USB HID
protocol. That protocol, and the per-key LED layout tables, were reverse
engineered by the OpenRGB project:

    OpenRGB - https://openrgb.org/
    Controllers/AsusAuraUSBController/AsusAuraTUFKeyboardController/
    Author: Mola19
    Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later

Because this project builds directly on that work, it is licensed under the same
terms. The derivation is recorded in the following places:

  * docs/PROTOCOL.md           the protocol as implemented here
  * include/claymore/protocol.hpp   packet layouts and mode numbering
  * src/layout_data.cpp        GENERATED from the OpenRGB layout header by
                               tools/gen_layout.py; do not edit by hand
  * src/device.cpp             firmware writes and sequence ordering

No OpenRGB source was copied verbatim; the packet builders are independent
implementations of the documented format, and the layout tables are extracted
mechanically so that their provenance stays auditable.
